WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.055
[MUSIC]

00:00:07.482 --> 00:00:12.620
Many reapplicants worry that they are at
a disadvantage to first time applicants.

00:00:12.620 --> 00:00:13.890
Is that true?

00:00:13.890 --> 00:00:16.340
And do you have any advice for
people who kind of reapply?

00:00:16.340 --> 00:00:17.570
&gt;&gt; We really read them fresh.

00:00:17.570 --> 00:00:21.410
So my best advise is, the person
who is evaluating your application

00:00:21.410 --> 00:00:23.090
likely is never seen it before.

00:00:23.090 --> 00:00:26.100
So there's no reason to explain
what's different or what's changed or

00:00:26.100 --> 00:00:29.480
maybe why you think you didn't get in,
some people will try to tell us that.

00:00:29.480 --> 00:00:31.660
Just start fresh and
look at what you've already submitted.

00:00:31.660 --> 00:00:33.110
You don't have to change everything, but

00:00:33.110 --> 00:00:36.650
think is there something at this moment
in time that could be more compelling.

00:00:36.650 --> 00:00:39.880
Perhaps in the last, or something you want
to change to be more representative of

00:00:39.880 --> 00:00:41.810
where I am at this moment.

00:00:41.810 --> 00:00:45.230
But please do, if you're committed
to Stanford reapply because there's

00:00:45.230 --> 00:00:48.290
a lot of students that we
admit from that category.

00:00:48.290 --> 00:00:50.370
&gt;&gt; Some of my favorite
classmates are reapplications.

00:00:50.370 --> 00:00:51.145
&gt;&gt; They told you.
[LAUGH]

00:00:51.145 --> 00:00:51.732
&gt;&gt; So I'm really glad-

00:00:51.732 --> 00:00:52.767
&gt;&gt; That's great.

00:00:52.767 --> 00:00:54.030
&gt;&gt; That they're here.

00:00:54.030 --> 00:00:54.902
&gt;&gt; That's awesome.

